gitrl-z (0.3.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Mark the reflog entry that was the newest one of its log when the window
    opened, with a "session start" pill before its message.
  * Keep the commit that HEAD was on at that moment in the graph, so the
    starting position stays visible when a reset in a terminal leaves it with
    no ref that reaches it.
  * Keep a copied command on the clipboard after gitrl-z stops, where the
    session has a clipboard manager.
  * Remove the Flatpak manifest. The AppImage, the PPA and the .deb are the
    supported distributions.

